      "writtenOn": "2025-08-19T18:51:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think there are reset/rewind functions we can use on these objects so we aren\u0027t re-allocating them every time we flush a Device. \n\nAlso, I believe in my WIP you started from, I\u0027d put these on the Device because I\u0027d been thinking that that was how managing the float storage manager would be easiest. Now that that is in the Recorder, I think it should be okay to reuse the KeyBuilder and data gatherer for every Device in a Recorder (exception being when we encounter an SkPictureShader or SkPictureImage during uniform extraction, so maybe Recorder has a stack of them that get checked out/returned to the recorder. Ideally we then have 1 set that reuses memory for almost every single draw, and occasionally we might have a 2nd one that is temporary).  Then we can just delete them at the end of snap() to prevent one unexpectedly large frame from holding on to too much memory (or re-allocate with the amount actually used in the prior frame, etc).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2108,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 2111,
        "endChar": 100
      },
      "revId": "e1a1c9967ecdb952d5b102f1a3b1c8f311c06f2d",
