    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "76590ce3_86fa2cc9",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/PipelineData.h",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 454,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-19T18:51:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Eventually the plan for uniform binding is to have a single binding to a struct/tuple that wraps the paint uniform definition and render step uniform definition.\n\nThe paint uniform fields would be declared first in this type, so their layout is unchanged regardless of the render steps that get combined afterwards. This means that in that world, the UniformManager can have a marked index/alignment-requirement for when the paint uniforms end and rewinding back for a new RS or draw just resets the index into its current storage.\n\nRight now that we have two bindings makes that approach a little more complicated because it\u0027d be nice to avoid the storage copying when restoring the RS changes but the RS collection isn\u0027t meant to depend on the prior alignment at all (so it\u0027s a little different than the existing support for pushing/popping structs).\n\nI think the simplest thing would be to add a second fUniformManager field to PipelineDataGatherer so that the paint uniforms that get collected can remain unmodified and uncopied while RS\u0027s or multiple draws are processed.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 449,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 454,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "e1a1c9967ecdb952d5b102f1a3b1c8f311c06f2d",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    }
